{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"53de6383b8484f22","name":"card_event_the_peoples_army","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/Homefront/events/card_event_the_peoples_army","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"THE PEOPLE'S ARMY","text":"Fill your hand and support line with LIGHT INFANTRY. Give them all Blitz.","flavorText":"As German forces drove deep into Soviet territory in 1941, the distinction between soldier and citizen effectively vanished. In cities like Leningrad, Moscow, and Stalingrad, millions of civilians were mobilized to fortify the motherland. Ordinary men and women took up shovels, picks, and axes to dig anti-tank ditches, assemble tank traps, and erect barricades. Students, factory workers, and pensioners labored around the clock, often under the direction of local party committees or driven by the sheer desperation of the approaching front. In Moscow alone, hundreds of thousands of civilians helped construct over 1,000 kilometers of defensive lines during the critical autumn of 1941. In besieged Leningrad, women and teenagers braved shellfire and bitter cold to repair roads, unload supplies, and tend to the wounded. This mass participation, often formalized as the People’s Militia, helped delay German offensives at key moments. Though untrained and often underfed, these civilians formed a vital support network, earning a reputation built not on rank or uniform, but on a shared resolve to survive.","faction":"Soviet","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":6,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_the_peoples_army","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_the_peoples_army_title","SourceString":"THE PEOPLE'S ARMY","LocalizedString":"THE PEOPLE'S ARMY"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":6,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_the_peoples_army_text","SourceString":"Fill your hand and support line with LIGHT IN