nsive lines during the critical autumn of 1941. In besieged Leningrad, women and teenagers braved shellfire and bitter cold to repair roads, unload supplies, and tend to the wounded. This mass participation, often formalized as the People’s Militia, helped delay German offensives at key moments. Though untrained and often underfed, these civilians formed a vital support network, earning a reputation built not on rank or uniform, but on a shared resolve to survive."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Homefront","spawnCardName":"card_unit_light_infantry","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Patriotic_Push'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/OrdersFeb17/Patriotic_Push.0"},"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/THE_PEOPLE_S_ARMY.THE_PEOPLE_S_ARMY","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":350.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_the_peoples_army_photo","SourceString":"Volunteers of the Moscow People's Militia conducting mortar drills in preparation for the defense of the capital, 1941.","LocalizedString":"Volunteers of the Moscow People's Militia conducting mortar drills in preparation for the defense of the capital, 1941."},"isAttackBuff":true,"isDefenseBuff":true},"variables":[{"name":"lightInfantries","type":"TArray<FName>","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_event_the_peoples_army","owner":"card_event_the_peoples_army_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"Temp_text_Variable","type":"FText","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Add_IntInt_ReturnValue","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_targetCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Variable_1","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"n